# Insights — Memory

*Last updated: {{YYYY-MM-DD}} (manual)*

> **Active lenses only** (Memory v2): ≤25 entries, ≤3 per primary subject, newest first. Each is a pattern worth re-reading in a year — not an observation about today, not a todo.
> - **Same pattern again → `evidence: N+1`** plus one journal `evidence` line. Never a second entry saying the same thing.
> - **New lens only if the novelty gate passes:** `python3 tools/memory_maint.py novelty --subject "#tag" --text "<title>. <body>"` (exit 0 = novel, exit 3 = near-duplicate of the lens it names). Subject already at 3? Supersede one first.
> - **Retire or supersede by metadata:** add `status: retired` or `status: superseded · superseded-by: I-NNNN` to the metadata line. The script moves the entry, full text intact, to `memory/archive/insights/YYYY-QN.md`. Never cut and paste between files.
> - Lenses help you frame and pick a lever. They are never a reason to skip a rule or to not log an event.
> - **3-year test:** if you wouldn't still find it useful in 3 years, it doesn't belong here.

